    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Hellenistic kingdom on the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#black-sea">Black Sea</a>, ruled by a dynasty of Persian origin from Amaseia and later Sinope.</li><li>Rich in metals, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#timber">timber</a> and Greek ports, it built a Black Sea empire under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI Eupator</a>.</li><li>Mithridates VI fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> in three wars from 89 to 63 BCE before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pompey">Pompey</a> destroyed the kingdom.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The geographer Strabo was born at Amaseia, the first Pontic capital, around 64 BCE, into a family that had served the kings of Pontus.</p></aside>
    </section>

